# Search Sheet

::summary
The universal search modal (F-3) — one centered sheet raised from the top-bar search button on every root (top 64px, `min(640px, 100vw − 20px)` wide, max-height capped). Input row (autofocused field · Find ⇄ Ask segmented-control · ✕), the seven-scope segmented strip (`search-scope` segmented-control, same idiom as `surfaces/search.surf`) with the raising surface pre-selecting its own segment, and the state body. ALL SIX reviewed states render inside this one modal — their full expression lives in `surfaces/search.surf`; the default open state is inlined below.
::

::modal[name=search title="Search" width=640 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::search[name=universal-search placeholder="Search this workspace…" action=runSearch]
:::

:::segmented-control[name=search-mode action=setSearchMode active=find size=compact]
- find "Find"
- ask "Ask Surfy"
:::

:::segmented-control[name=search-scope action=setSearchScope active=everything size=compact]
- everything "Everything"
- docs "Docs"
- tasks "Tasks"
- apps "Apps"
- messages "Messages"
- files "Files"
- devices "Devices"
:::

Find matches across the workspace, or Ask Surfy for a grounded answer.

:::toolbar
- text[value="RECENT"]
:::

:::row[icon=doc action=openRecent href=#]
Talent
Opened 1h ago
:::

:::row[icon=task action=openRecent href=#]
Gather Donovan's account details and failure mode
Viewed 2h ago
:::

:::row[icon=sparkle action=openRecent href=#]
tidepool
Deployed · tidepool.surf.space
:::

::

Esc dismisses; top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. The six states (open-from-Docs recents, Everything recents, Find results, Find no-match, Ask idle, Ask answered) and the scope pre-selection map: `surfaces/search.surf`. A hit or recent routes to its surface and closes the sheet; Ask's Continue in Surfy seeds the panel composer, never auto-sends.

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
